**Given:**

Practical marks for subject 1: 40

Theory marks for subject 1: 110

Practical marks for subject 2: 60

Theory marks for subject 2: 40

Average practical marks: 40

Average theory marks: 60

**Calculation:**

We have:

⇒ Total practical marks = 40 + 60 = 100

⇒ Total theory marks = 110 + 40 = 150

⇒ Total marks obtained by R = (Average practical marks × Number of subjects) + (Average theory marks × Number of subjects)

⇒ Total marks obtained by R = (40 × 2) + (60 × 2)

⇒ Total marks obtained by R = 80 + 120 = 200

⇒ Number of subjects = 2

Hence,

⇒ Average marks per subject = Total marks obtained by R / Number of subjects

⇒ Average marks per subject = 200 / 2

⇒ Average marks per subject = 100

**∴ The average marks per subject are 100.**
